; SP 800_90A's CTR_DRBG UPDATE  section 10 point 2 point 1 point 2  for
; AES_128 with NO derivation function  where seedlen is thirty two bytes;
;
;   temp is AES of K over V stepped once  then over V stepped twice
;   temp = temp exclusive or provided_data
;   K = temp's first sixteen bytes   V = its last sixteen
;
; TWO CIPHER RUNS WRITTEN AS A LOOP OF TWO  and that is not tidiness; each
; include of block/aes128encrypt is about a hundred and seventy six thousand
; instructions of PROGRAM TEXT  and this block is itself included twice  so
; writing the two runs out would put four copies in the file where there are
; now two; The generate loop next door holds the third and last;
;
; THE LOOP BODY CAN BE THE SAME BOTH TIMES because everything that differs
; between the two halves is on a CONVEYOR; provided_data is thirty two cells
; that give up their head and slide  and the answer is thirty two cells that
; slide and take a new tail; So the first turn consumes bytes nought to
; fifteen and the second sixteen to thirty one  without either turn knowing
; which it is;
;
; AND THE PROVIDED DATA IS SPENT  which is what makes the trailing update
; free: the instantiate call consumes the entropy into the exclusive or  so
; those thirty two cells are already nought when the second call runs  and
; exclusive or with nought is what SP 800_90A asks for there;
;
; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE; this block is included at offset nought twice  so
; they resolve to the addresses its caller's tape map names;
;
; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero  which is its caller's)
;   @0x000:0x374  the cipher's frame
;   @0x375:0x384  K{16}   the generator's key  replaced at the end
;   @0x385:0x3a4  OUT{32} the answer  filled tail first over thirty two turns
;   @0x3a5:0x3c4  PRV{32} provided data  SPENT
;   @0x3c7:0x3d6  V{16}   the counter  stepped twice  replaced at the end
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
R1044
  ++
; ASSERT ptr=+1044
[
  -
; the counter steps by one
L77
%%block/inc128%% 967
; ASSERT ptr=+983
; SP 800_90A defines the counter modulo two to the hundred and twenty
; eighth  so a wrap is not an error here and the carry is dropped; that
; is the one place this differs from counter mode  which is out of
; keystream when it wraps
  [-]
; ==== the counter is enciphered ====
; the window holds the tenth round key and the constant holds 0x6c  so
; both are put back before every run  as block/aes128encrypt's own
; contract requires
L983
  [-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]
  R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]R1[-]
R30
  [-]
L45
; ASSERT zero +0:+116
; the key is COPIED  because every run wants it again
R885
%%block/copy16%% 885
L884
%%block/copy16back%% 16
; and so is the counter  which the increment wants again
R936
%%block/copy16%% 967
L884
%%block/copy16back%% 98
L68
